1
00:00:14,230 --> 00:00:17,150
I see. That is a grave illness.

2
00:00:17,150 --> 00:00:20,720
It's remarkable that you've 
endured this long without dying.

3
00:00:20,720 --> 00:00:22,550
Wh-Who are you?!

4
00:00:34,810 --> 00:00:38,030
You don't even know how to 
vent your accumulated mana?

5
00:00:38,590 --> 00:00:41,280
Your lack of understanding 
is truly lamentable.

6
00:01:08,950 --> 00:01:12,510
How's that? Do you feel a bit better?

7
00:01:12,680 --> 00:01:15,030
Wh-What have you done?

8
00:01:15,030 --> 00:01:16,850
How could a young lady...

9
00:01:17,700 --> 00:01:20,350
I only sucked out your mana directly.

10
00:01:21,500 --> 00:01:22,350
Mana?

11
00:01:22,570 --> 00:01:25,280
What you have is not a disease.

12
00:01:25,280 --> 00:01:26,960
It's called the Magic Release Period.

13
00:01:27,410 --> 00:01:29,310
Magic... Release Period?

14
00:01:29,720 --> 00:01:31,680
It is extremely rare.

15
00:01:32,050 --> 00:01:36,020
I'm sure no one has ever 
understood you because of it.

16
00:01:37,300 --> 00:01:40,880
But I understand your suffering...

17
00:01:40,880 --> 00:01:43,620
as one who has experienced 
the same feelings.

18
00:01:58,500 --> 00:01:59,950
But who are you?

19
00:02:00,610 --> 00:02:02,270
I am a witch.

20
00:02:03,210 --> 00:02:06,680
An evil witch who occasionally 
does nice things.

21
00:02:08,050 --> 00:02:08,990
And you?

22
00:02:15,490 --> 00:02:18,650
Well, Betty? What do you think of the 
romance between our teacher and myself?

23
00:02:18,650 --> 00:02:20,130
There's nothing to think.

24
00:02:20,130 --> 00:02:23,160
I didn't hear a single, 
solitary thing about it, I suppose.

25
00:02:23,500 --> 00:02:27,120
Also, "romance"? You're being 
far too familiar toward Mother.

26
00:02:27,120 --> 00:02:29,490
You're right. It was just 
an excuse to say it.

27
00:02:29,490 --> 00:02:33,700
But I still remember every 
word she said that day.

28
00:02:33,700 --> 00:02:36,500
That would cause nothing but 
trouble for Mother, I suppose.

29
00:02:36,500 --> 00:02:39,060
And for me, too, of course.

30
00:02:39,060 --> 00:02:42,340
Beatrice-sama, you shouldn't 
say things like that.

31
00:02:42,700 --> 00:02:46,820
Also, I can understand 
how Roswaal-sama feels,

32
00:02:46,820 --> 00:02:50,190
as someone else who was 
saved by Echidna-sama.

33
00:02:52,690 --> 00:02:55,730
You must be grateful to 
her as well, Ryuzu-kun.

34
00:02:55,730 --> 00:02:56,570
Yes.

35
00:02:56,980 --> 00:03:00,340
If I hadn't met her that day,

36
00:03:00,340 --> 00:03:02,880
I would still be suffering alone now.

37
00:03:03,530 --> 00:03:08,290
Either that or, in my despair, 
I might have done something rash.

38
00:03:08,660 --> 00:03:13,860
Instead, I bested my parents and siblings 
to overtake the Mathers family,

39
00:03:14,510 --> 00:03:16,500
all thanks to her.

40
00:03:16,800 --> 00:03:19,440
Hah! What a shameless 
man you are, I suppose!

41
00:03:19,440 --> 00:03:22,400
It's cowardly to coerce 
someone into being grateful!

42
00:03:22,400 --> 00:03:27,770
But you often say things like, 
"You'd better be grateful."

43
00:03:27,770 --> 00:03:30,980
Hey! Are you on my side 
or Roswaal's, I suppose?!

44
00:03:33,950 --> 00:03:38,210
You know, I don't like that 
lukewarm look in your eyes.

45
00:03:38,210 --> 00:03:40,770
If there's something you want 
to say, then say it, I suppose.

46
00:03:40,770 --> 00:03:42,730
Well, I love you.

47
00:03:42,730 --> 00:03:45,330
Don't say disgusting things like that!

48
00:03:46,980 --> 00:03:48,020
Teacher!

49
00:03:48,370 --> 00:03:50,120
All three of you are here?

50
00:03:50,580 --> 00:03:53,250
Good. Have you been getting 
along and not fighting?

51
00:03:53,470 --> 00:03:54,520
Of course!

52
00:03:54,520 --> 00:03:55,740
Naturally, I suppose.

53
00:03:58,610 --> 00:04:00,020
Goodness.

54
00:04:00,020 --> 00:04:03,300
Looks like you're all still quite a handful.

55
00:04:07,040 --> 00:04:10,680
Oh? So you heard that story?

56
00:04:10,980 --> 00:04:15,400
Yeah. They're the memories of Ryuzu Meyer 
that Shima-san saw in the graveyard.

57
00:04:15,700 --> 00:04:17,140
I see.

58
00:04:17,140 --> 00:04:21,360
That would mean you now know what 
happened that day, too...

59
00:04:22,470 --> 00:04:26,320
The day this Sanctuary was born.

60
00:04:28,100 --> 00:04:31,580
Really, that Roswaal is 
so irritating, I suppose!

61
00:04:31,920 --> 00:04:33,890
He's utterly intolerable!

62
00:04:33,890 --> 00:04:40,960
I think Roswaal-sama was only avenging 
me because you were being mean to me.

63
00:04:41,270 --> 00:04:44,220
D-Don't say I was being mean, I suppose!

64
00:04:44,220 --> 00:04:46,720
It was much more refined than that!

65
00:04:46,970 --> 00:04:49,720
No matter how many doors I opened, 
they led to the same room.

66
00:04:49,720 --> 00:04:52,930
It was a very frightening experience for me.

67
00:04:53,760 --> 00:04:56,620
It was just a bit of yin magic, I suppose.

68
00:04:56,620 --> 00:04:59,120
There's nothing to get so 
bent out of shape about.

69
00:04:59,490 --> 00:05:00,420
I see.

70
00:05:00,850 --> 00:05:04,950
So even though I did the exact same 
thing to you with yang magic,

71
00:05:05,250 --> 00:05:07,410
you won't get bent out of shape.

72
00:05:07,680 --> 00:05:08,540
Ngh!

73
00:05:09,300 --> 00:05:11,550
What a great expression, Beatrice.

74
00:05:11,990 --> 00:05:15,860
Your face is my second favorite 
behind our teacher's, you know.

75
00:05:15,860 --> 00:05:17,670
What do you think you're saying?!

76
00:05:18,050 --> 00:05:20,830
You're just some lucky guy who was 
blessed with talent and a good family,

77
00:05:20,830 --> 00:05:23,920
who just happened to find the best 
teacher in the world, I suppose!

78
00:05:23,920 --> 00:05:25,420
Don't let it go to your head!

79
00:05:25,660 --> 00:05:29,110
Beatrice-sama, I think you're 
just complimenting him.

80
00:05:29,110 --> 00:05:33,740
Ryuzu-kun, if Beatrice ever bothers 
you again, just come to me.

81
00:05:33,740 --> 00:05:36,960
I'll spank her bottom to teach her a lesson.

82
00:05:36,960 --> 00:05:41,400
Hah! This girl will never 
rely on you, I suppose!

83
00:05:41,400 --> 00:05:43,150
Go on, tell him!

84
00:05:43,530 --> 00:05:45,140
Thank you.

85
00:05:45,140 --> 00:05:48,240
If anything happens, I will 
certainly let you know.

86
00:05:48,560 --> 00:05:50,710
How dare you, I suppose?!

87
00:05:50,710 --> 00:05:51,700
Hmph!

88
00:05:52,850 --> 00:05:54,970
Sorry I interrupted your reading.

89
00:05:54,970 --> 00:05:57,220
I apologize on behalf of Beatrice.

90
00:05:57,220 --> 00:05:59,670
Please, don't concern yourself with that.

91
00:05:59,930 --> 00:06:03,480
I can't exactly call this 
"reading" yet, anyway.

92
00:06:04,030 --> 00:06:07,300
Hmm... Reading books is 
a good thing, I suppose.

93
00:06:07,730 --> 00:06:10,440
Reading makes your life richer.

94
00:06:10,440 --> 00:06:14,310
So said Beatrice as she echoed the 
very same words her teacher used.

95
00:06:14,640 --> 00:06:15,810
Grr!

96
00:06:16,590 --> 00:06:17,850
Oh, I know.

97
00:06:17,850 --> 00:06:22,220
Beatrice, why don't you 
become Ryuzu-kun's teacher?

98
00:06:22,220 --> 00:06:24,450
Me? Teach her?

99
00:06:24,450 --> 00:06:29,830
I-I couldn't trouble Beatrice-sama 
with that when she's so busy.

100
00:06:29,830 --> 00:06:32,860
N-Now, I didn't say I wasn't 
willing, I suppose.

101
00:06:33,220 --> 00:06:35,580
It would be a simple task.

102
00:06:37,490 --> 00:06:41,110
What, I suppose? If you don't 
want to, you don't have to.

103
00:06:41,110 --> 00:06:42,870
It's not as if I'm all that enthus—

104
00:06:42,870 --> 00:06:43,460
Oh, no!

105
00:06:43,860 --> 00:06:48,420
It would make me very happy 
to have you teach me.

106
00:06:49,400 --> 00:06:52,840
W-Well, if you insist, 
then I have no choice, I suppose.

107
00:06:52,840 --> 00:06:55,360
You really are one lucky girl.

108
00:06:59,700 --> 00:07:01,180
Beatrice-sama?

109
00:07:01,600 --> 00:07:03,500
Mother is calling, I suppose.

110
00:07:06,690 --> 00:07:10,010
Roswaal! Mother is calling for you, too!

111
00:07:10,010 --> 00:07:11,320
It's urgent, I suppose!

112
00:07:11,930 --> 00:07:12,940
I know!

113
00:07:13,310 --> 00:07:16,540
It seems... he is here.

114
00:07:24,830 --> 00:07:26,300
I have confirmation.

115
00:07:26,680 --> 00:07:28,130
It is definitely him.

116
00:07:29,110 --> 00:07:30,060
I see.

117
00:07:30,590 --> 00:07:32,530
We should flee from here immediately!

118
00:07:32,530 --> 00:07:35,170
If he comes here, our plan will fail,

119
00:07:35,170 --> 00:07:36,760
and it will be impossible to start over!

120
00:07:38,970 --> 00:07:41,730
Teacher! There is no time for hesitation!

121
00:07:41,730 --> 00:07:44,440
I cannot be of any use to you yet.

122
00:07:44,440 --> 00:07:47,270
If you ask me to be your shield,
 I will gladly do so!

123
00:07:47,580 --> 00:07:49,680
But if we fail to take countermeasures...

124
00:07:51,360 --> 00:07:53,440
It's not as if there's nothing we can do.

125
00:07:53,440 --> 00:07:56,240
The plans for the Sanctuary 
are in place, to an extent.

126
00:07:58,110 --> 00:08:00,480
Construction of the theory is complete.

127
00:08:00,480 --> 00:08:01,780
Th-Then...

128
00:08:01,780 --> 00:08:06,610
But we still lack the core 
necessary for generating the barrier.

129
00:08:06,610 --> 00:08:09,000
Without it, the barrier won't function.

130
00:08:09,420 --> 00:08:11,310
All the work we've done...

131
00:08:12,620 --> 00:08:16,180
The Sanctuary was just one 
step away from completion!

132
00:08:20,370 --> 00:08:23,980
Um... For this core that 
you don't have yet...

133
00:08:26,310 --> 00:08:28,680
Could I be of any use?

134
00:08:30,180 --> 00:08:31,150
Ryuzu-kun...

135
00:08:31,550 --> 00:08:34,340
I've heard about it already.

136
00:08:34,340 --> 00:08:40,130
The one who meets the requirements to be 
the core for Echidna-sama's barrier is me.

137
00:08:40,130 --> 00:08:42,000
Did Beatrice tell you that?

138
00:08:43,090 --> 00:08:43,960
Yes.

139
00:08:45,190 --> 00:08:50,400
It's true that there's a good chance you 
would function as the barrier's core,

140
00:08:50,400 --> 00:08:54,760
but only after your mana and 
the land adapt to one another.

141
00:08:54,760 --> 00:08:57,200
So I can't do it right now?

142
00:08:57,200 --> 00:08:59,430
This is no ordinary barrier.

143
00:08:59,430 --> 00:09:03,350
We spent years gathering people with 
mixed human and demihuman blood here

144
00:09:03,350 --> 00:09:05,730
on a scale large enough 
to activate the barrier.

145
00:09:05,730 --> 00:09:08,400
You are the last push needed to complete it.

146
00:09:09,030 --> 00:09:09,950
But...

147
00:09:15,490 --> 00:09:20,060
I'm sure the two of you have 
a way to make it work, yes?

148
00:09:21,700 --> 00:09:25,790
Echidna-sama and Roswaal-sama, 
the two of you saved me.

149
00:09:26,450 --> 00:09:31,750
I've been so happy to live without 
being ostracized or looked down upon.

150
00:09:32,190 --> 00:09:34,700
If I can repay you for the time 
I've had to live this way,

151
00:09:35,090 --> 00:09:39,030
I believe that would give my life meaning.

152
00:09:43,760 --> 00:09:44,560
Teacher...

153
00:09:45,920 --> 00:09:49,670
We will use your od as the catalyst 
to make the Sanctuary's core.

154
00:09:50,280 --> 00:09:55,030
That should shorten the process and 
allow the barrier to function.

155
00:09:55,250 --> 00:09:58,030
And then the Sanctuary will be saved?

156
00:09:58,030 --> 00:10:01,050
It will make it possible to 
drive away the current threat.

157
00:10:02,170 --> 00:10:04,490
When would you get started?

158
00:10:04,770 --> 00:10:06,220
Right away.

159
00:10:06,740 --> 00:10:10,610
I'm having Beatrice prepare the location 
where the core will be placed.

160
00:10:10,610 --> 00:10:14,290
All I would need is enough 
time to construct the spell.

161
00:10:14,290 --> 00:10:16,550
And that is my job, correct?

162
00:10:17,520 --> 00:10:20,760
I will do everything in 
my power to buy time.

163
00:10:21,360 --> 00:10:23,730
Ryuzu-kun, I'm sorry.

164
00:10:23,730 --> 00:10:27,370
My strength alone is insufficient 
to protect our teacher.

165
00:10:27,370 --> 00:10:31,980
No, you have also given 
me so much, Roswaal-sama.

166
00:10:32,610 --> 00:10:34,770
If anything, I am truly grateful.

167
00:10:34,770 --> 00:10:37,190
I have no reason to resent you.

168
00:10:39,630 --> 00:10:40,940
I will go at once.

169
00:10:41,330 --> 00:10:44,950
Teacher, please prepare the barrier 
and call Beatrice back here.

170
00:10:46,160 --> 00:10:49,260
Perhaps we shouldn't let 
Beatrice know about this?

171
00:10:49,260 --> 00:10:51,730
If we don't call Beatrice back right now,

172
00:10:51,730 --> 00:10:54,420
she will despise both you and me forever.

173
00:10:55,780 --> 00:10:58,420
Of course, she might do that 
even if we do call her...

174
00:10:59,460 --> 00:11:02,000
Very well. I'll take your advice.

175
00:11:15,990 --> 00:11:17,550
Beatrice-sama...

176
00:11:31,420 --> 00:11:33,290
You still want to keep going?

177
00:11:35,290 --> 00:11:36,800
Shut up.

178
00:11:36,800 --> 00:11:37,960
You're too noisy.

179
00:11:37,960 --> 00:11:39,090
You're annoying me.

180
00:11:39,090 --> 00:11:40,340
You're a pain in the ass.

181
00:11:40,340 --> 00:11:41,220
I'm losing interest.

182
00:11:41,220 --> 00:11:42,130
I'm losing heart.

183
00:11:43,180 --> 00:11:47,960
I... I have to stop you... here.

184
00:11:49,520 --> 00:11:51,410
I really hate this.

185
00:11:51,410 --> 00:11:52,640
It's bringing me down so much.

186
00:11:53,200 --> 00:11:55,890
I'm so sad... so distraught...

187
00:11:55,890 --> 00:11:59,510
This is the worst of the 
worst of the worst.

188
00:11:59,510 --> 00:12:00,570
So depressing.

189
00:12:07,260 --> 00:12:08,990
Is someone there?

190
00:12:12,930 --> 00:12:14,330
So depressing.

191
00:12:16,560 --> 00:12:19,840
Al Goa!

192
00:12:22,110 --> 00:12:24,930
Getting sweaty annoys me so much.

193
00:12:26,110 --> 00:12:28,970
Damn you, Devil of Melancholy!

194
00:12:29,200 --> 00:12:31,060
I hate that name.

195
00:12:31,060 --> 00:12:32,750
It crushes my spirit.

196
00:12:33,090 --> 00:12:37,530
Do you think I ended up like 
this because I wanted to?

197
00:12:37,530 --> 00:12:41,200
No matter how you try to 
twist the way you live,

198
00:12:41,200 --> 00:12:45,910
you're the one who chose the life you 
have now from among limited choices!

199
00:12:45,910 --> 00:12:48,720
Don't you dare play the victim...

200
00:12:48,720 --> 00:12:51,880
Devil of Melancholy, Hector!

201
00:12:52,300 --> 00:12:55,890
Your correct statement makes me 
feel hurt and uncomfortable.

202
00:12:55,890 --> 00:12:59,960
I really just can't stand you at all.

203
00:13:04,760 --> 00:13:07,720
Your bones are crushed, 
your organs are splattered,

204
00:13:07,720 --> 00:13:09,570
your heart is splintered.

205
00:13:09,570 --> 00:13:12,810
With that out of the way, how about now?

206
00:13:14,920 --> 00:13:19,020
I suppose it would be a stretch 
to say I made it in time.

207
00:13:19,370 --> 00:13:22,080
No, you are right on time.

208
00:13:22,660 --> 00:13:29,840
Your pupil fought bravely to 
keep me here and buy you time.

209
00:13:29,840 --> 00:13:32,240
This hurts more than I expected.

210
00:13:32,240 --> 00:13:35,840
If you want to cry, 
shall we set aside time for it?

211
00:13:35,840 --> 00:13:38,060
You haven't changed a bit, have you?

212
00:13:38,060 --> 00:13:40,180
You're exactly how you 
were when we parted ways.

213
00:13:40,180 --> 00:13:43,670
And just like then, you still 
don't know how to talk to me.

214
00:13:44,000 --> 00:13:48,340
You were so adorable back then, though.

215
00:13:53,180 --> 00:13:57,010
How long are you going to lie there 
looking pathetic, I suppose?

216
00:13:57,310 --> 00:13:59,720
Huh? Beatrice-sama?

217
00:13:59,720 --> 00:14:04,130
Stop spacing out. We need to move 
while Mother is buying us time.

218
00:14:04,130 --> 00:14:05,440
B-But...

219
00:14:06,860 --> 00:14:08,970
The preparations are complete.

220
00:14:08,970 --> 00:14:11,160
That's what Mother said, I suppose.

221
00:14:13,760 --> 00:14:15,030
All right.

222
00:14:15,490 --> 00:14:17,620
Let's go, Beatrice-sama.

223
00:14:31,210 --> 00:14:34,020
If you don't want to become 
a part of this crystal,

224
00:14:34,020 --> 00:14:36,020
don't just stand there 
staring mindlessly at it.

225
00:14:36,290 --> 00:14:39,070
I'm sorry... I know this isn't the time.

226
00:14:39,520 --> 00:14:41,570
So what now, I suppose?

227
00:14:41,570 --> 00:14:46,030
Mother told me to bring you here,
 but nothing beyond that.

228
00:14:47,030 --> 00:14:52,380
Yet you can still do as 
Echidna-sama tells you.

229
00:14:52,380 --> 00:14:53,740
Of course, I suppose.

230
00:14:54,120 --> 00:14:56,840
To me, Mother is absolute.

231
00:14:57,780 --> 00:15:00,960
You and the people living 
here are truly blessed.

232
00:15:01,460 --> 00:15:03,570
Once this is all taken care of,

233
00:15:03,570 --> 00:15:06,270
you can repay that by working 
your hardest, I suppose.

234
00:15:11,380 --> 00:15:14,720
You're smiling, but that's not 
an agreeable look on your face.

235
00:15:21,940 --> 00:15:25,900
I-I'm sorry! Something got into my eye.

236
00:15:27,490 --> 00:15:31,140
Actually, you just stay here and 
don't do anything, I suppose.

237
00:15:31,140 --> 00:15:33,970
I'm going to help Mother.

238
00:15:33,970 --> 00:15:38,200
I also need to save Roswaal before 
he ends up dead, I suppose.

239
00:15:38,200 --> 00:15:40,320
So from tomorrow on...

240
00:15:43,320 --> 00:15:48,090
Beatrice-sama, thank you for everything 
you've done over all this time.

241
00:15:48,390 --> 00:15:49,050
Huh?

242
00:15:49,840 --> 00:15:51,900
It's time to say goodbye.

243
00:15:52,370 --> 00:15:55,060
What do you mean by "goodbye"?

244
00:15:55,060 --> 00:15:59,880
This facility has been prepared to 
place a barrier over the forest.

245
00:15:59,880 --> 00:16:03,270
I was to spend time activating 
the barrier as its core...

246
00:16:03,620 --> 00:16:06,730
But the time I have is no longer enough.

247
00:16:07,080 --> 00:16:09,560
Time... for the barrier?

248
00:16:09,560 --> 00:16:12,130
I-If that man is interfering, I'll—

249
00:16:12,130 --> 00:16:14,110
You can't win just by fighting him.

250
00:16:14,110 --> 00:16:15,820
That's what the Sanctuary is for.

251
00:16:16,290 --> 00:16:19,150
That's why Roswaal-sama 
has sacrificed so much.

252
00:16:19,150 --> 00:16:23,100
Because he knows he can't 
save Echidna-sama otherwise.

253
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:27,200
If we can just complete the barrier, 
we can protect this place.

254
00:16:27,910 --> 00:16:30,710
I will offer myself up for that purpose.

255
00:16:31,520 --> 00:16:33,820
Don't say such ridiculous things!

256
00:16:33,820 --> 00:16:35,520
You'll offer yourself up?

257
00:16:35,520 --> 00:16:39,210
You don't even know magic! 
What can you do, I suppose?!

258
00:16:39,210 --> 00:16:39,850
You can't—

259
00:16:44,610 --> 00:16:47,290
This magic crystal will be the catalyst

260
00:16:47,290 --> 00:16:50,100
to form the barrier using 
your od as the core?

261
00:16:50,980 --> 00:16:54,820
Yes. That was Echidna-sama's idea.

262
00:16:55,720 --> 00:16:57,650
Wait! You're wrong!

263
00:16:57,650 --> 00:17:01,080
I'll go talk to Mother about it 
myself right now, I suppose!

264
00:17:01,080 --> 00:17:03,970
Mother dotes on me! I know she'll lis—

265
00:17:03,970 --> 00:17:05,890
We don't have that much time.

266
00:17:05,890 --> 00:17:08,540
The decision has to be made right now.

267
00:17:08,830 --> 00:17:12,950
Then my decision is that I'm 
going to go help Mother!

268
00:17:12,950 --> 00:17:16,590
Together, Mother and I can 
beat him easily, I suppose!

269
00:17:19,240 --> 00:17:23,310
Everyone can just run away from 
here through my Door Crossing.

270
00:17:25,220 --> 00:17:27,600
Right? I'll do that, I suppose!

271
00:17:27,600 --> 00:17:30,100
It will be hard on me with so many people,

272
00:17:30,100 --> 00:17:32,160
but I can pull it off!

273
00:17:32,160 --> 00:17:36,050
And I'll find an opening to grab Roswaal 
and get Mother away, I suppose!

274
00:17:36,050 --> 00:17:37,530
See? That will—

275
00:17:41,670 --> 00:17:46,080
Do you want to live your life running away,
 afraid of being chased again?

276
00:17:46,820 --> 00:17:49,650
We finally have a place 
where we can enjoy peace,

277
00:17:49,650 --> 00:17:52,130
thanks to Echidna-sama and Roswaal-sama.

278
00:17:52,480 --> 00:17:57,860
If we abandon it, how long will 
it take to build a new Sanctuary?

279
00:17:58,900 --> 00:18:03,100
I've been granted more than enough 
time to enjoy warmth and kindness.

280
00:18:04,050 --> 00:18:06,100
I love this place.

281
00:18:06,590 --> 00:18:09,660
I'm truly happy that I was able to live here.

282
00:18:10,180 --> 00:18:13,520
I love the smiles of 
everyone who lives here.

283
00:18:14,640 --> 00:18:17,070
I don't want to lose them.

284
00:18:18,680 --> 00:18:21,870
No matter what you think about this place,

285
00:18:21,870 --> 00:18:24,820
it doesn't exist for people like you!

286
00:18:24,820 --> 00:18:26,960
Yes, I know.

287
00:18:28,290 --> 00:18:32,640
Then... If you know that, then why?!

288
00:18:34,210 --> 00:18:35,490
It's all right.

289
00:18:35,490 --> 00:18:37,880
That may have been true in the beginning.

290
00:18:38,740 --> 00:18:39,470
But...

291
00:18:40,800 --> 00:18:44,040
There's no way all of the time we spent here

292
00:18:44,040 --> 00:18:46,640
can stay as it was in the beginning.

293
00:18:47,640 --> 00:18:49,680
The choice to live here,

294
00:18:49,680 --> 00:18:52,110
and the choice to talk with you,

295
00:18:52,110 --> 00:18:56,090
were all choices I made on my own.

296
00:18:57,240 --> 00:19:00,320
I haven't lost anything.

297
00:19:01,010 --> 00:19:04,230
I still have everything I've been given.

298
00:19:05,550 --> 00:19:07,710
Living here made me happy.

299
00:19:08,130 --> 00:19:12,670
So to protect all of those times... I must go.

300
00:19:13,590 --> 00:19:20,880
I offer my affection and gratitude to you,
 Beatrice-sama, over and over again.

301
00:19:29,090 --> 00:19:30,270
Beatrice-sama...

302
00:19:33,230 --> 00:19:37,020
Be careful not to eat too many sweets.

303
00:19:49,440 --> 00:19:51,370
Th-The books...

304
00:19:52,450 --> 00:19:55,590
I promised to teach you 
how to read and write.

305
00:20:08,470 --> 00:20:09,580
Thank you.

306
00:20:23,990 --> 00:20:24,950
Goodbye,

307
00:20:25,840 --> 00:20:26,800
Betty.

308
00:20:32,320 --> 00:20:36,130
And that's everything I was told.

309
00:20:37,240 --> 00:20:38,430
And?

310
00:20:38,800 --> 00:20:43,160
Assuming that story is true, what of it?

311
00:20:43,770 --> 00:20:46,050
I'll say it again! Surrender!

312
00:20:46,430 --> 00:20:48,350
The course of events has changed.

313
00:20:48,350 --> 00:20:50,490
Stop the people you sent to the mansion.

314
00:20:50,490 --> 00:20:52,680
Then all of this can be reconciled!

315
00:20:54,630 --> 00:20:56,560
I refuse, Subaru-kun.

316
00:20:57,380 --> 00:21:02,320
I didn't come through these 400 years 
only to bend to a change of this degree.

317
00:21:02,690 --> 00:21:04,870
If you think bringing in a 
pawn from outside the board

318
00:21:04,870 --> 00:21:09,630
and removing Garfiel gives you an advantage,
 you are very mistaken.

319
00:21:09,630 --> 00:21:10,720
What?!

320
00:21:10,720 --> 00:21:12,080
Am I wrong?

321
00:21:12,510 --> 00:21:15,980
You snapped so vigorously 
at outsiders before,

322
00:21:15,980 --> 00:21:20,020
and now you're one of Subaru-kun's 
merry band of friends.

323
00:21:20,020 --> 00:21:23,260
I am quite surprised at how 
quickly you changed your tune.

324
00:21:23,260 --> 00:21:27,090
Heh! Nothin' you say carries 
any weight, Roswaal!

325
00:21:28,080 --> 00:21:29,530
Carries no weight...

326
00:21:30,220 --> 00:21:34,570
After clinging to one desire every 
day for the past ten years,

327
00:21:34,570 --> 00:21:37,890
then letting it go with such ease,
 you say <i>I</i> carry no weight?

328
00:21:37,890 --> 00:21:39,560
What a pathetic joke.

329
00:21:40,750 --> 00:21:43,120
A wish does not simply go away.

330
00:21:43,120 --> 00:21:46,700
If you truly loved your mother and family,

331
00:21:46,700 --> 00:21:48,540
if you loved them that much,

332
00:21:48,540 --> 00:21:51,530
would you really change so readily?

333
00:21:51,860 --> 00:21:56,480
Or did you not love your 
mother and family at all?

334
00:21:56,820 --> 00:22:00,080
Is a wish that folded the moment 
your fangs were broken off

335
00:22:00,080 --> 00:22:02,500
what you spent your last ten years on?

336
00:22:02,810 --> 00:22:04,770
Don't get the wrong idea.

337
00:22:05,510 --> 00:22:06,760
The wrong idea?

338
00:22:07,090 --> 00:22:12,140
I didn't just decide to follow my 
boss 'cause he beat me in a fight.

339
00:22:12,810 --> 00:22:16,020
I spent ten years clingin' to the past.

340
00:22:16,290 --> 00:22:19,980
I just faced that past for 
the first time in ten years.

341
00:22:20,250 --> 00:22:23,230
You confronted your past? You?

342
00:22:23,480 --> 00:22:29,030
I ain't interested in tellin' you what I saw 
there or why I started followin' my boss.

343
00:22:29,480 --> 00:22:36,500
But I will tell you the one big reason 
I decided to follow him instead of you.

344
00:22:38,340 --> 00:22:42,020
'Cause rather than the one who 
told me to stay weak forever,

345
00:22:42,480 --> 00:22:47,970
why wouldn't I follow the one who says, 
"I need you because you're strong"?

346
00:22:49,430 --> 00:22:51,680
Huh? What?!

347
00:22:51,680 --> 00:22:55,140
Oh, nothing. I'm counting on you, man.

348
00:22:57,770 --> 00:23:00,080
Garfiel saw the past.

349
00:23:00,080 --> 00:23:02,030
Even if he's standing here as a result,

350
00:23:02,480 --> 00:23:06,650
that doesn't mean the love he had for 
his family for ten years is any weaker.

351
00:23:07,110 --> 00:23:09,560
The strength of his feelings hasn't changed.

352
00:23:10,160 --> 00:23:13,070
He changed without ever changing.

353
00:23:14,480 --> 00:23:16,270
The same goes for you.

354
00:23:16,270 --> 00:23:20,000
If your methods... If you were just 
facing the same direction as us,

355
00:23:20,000 --> 00:23:21,460
we could get along.

356
00:23:21,920 --> 00:23:23,750
It's not too late to turn back!

357
00:23:26,400 --> 00:23:29,190
I still have the advantage.

358
00:23:29,190 --> 00:23:30,570
What?

359
00:23:30,570 --> 00:23:34,400
Per the terms of our wager, 
your greatest weapon was bound,

360
00:23:34,400 --> 00:23:36,350
making you an ordinary person.

361
00:23:36,350 --> 00:23:39,510
And what can an ordinary person like you do?

362
00:23:39,510 --> 00:23:41,140
You cannot do anything!

363
00:23:41,470 --> 00:23:43,010
Nothing at all!

364
00:23:43,010 --> 00:23:45,600
You are less than ordinary! 
What can you do?!

365
00:23:45,600 --> 00:23:49,380
In the Sanctuary, no one can violate 
the feelings carved into you by time!

366
00:23:49,380 --> 00:23:51,830
No one! That will never change!

367
00:23:51,830 --> 00:23:57,540
My 400 years will never be overturned 
by an ordinary person like you!

368
00:23:58,250 --> 00:24:00,500
Because feelings don't change?

369
00:24:00,690 --> 00:24:01,370
Yes!

370
00:24:01,580 --> 00:24:05,230
Because it's what you've 
believed for so long?

371
00:24:05,230 --> 00:24:06,880
Yes, that's right!

372
00:24:06,880 --> 00:24:11,380
Why don't you ever look at anything 
but the weakness of feelings?!

373
00:24:11,380 --> 00:24:15,730
You know that caring about someone 
for a long time is a strong feeling!

374
00:24:15,730 --> 00:24:18,470
Why do you only try to 
see the weakness in it?!

375
00:24:18,470 --> 00:24:22,060
Because that is what I believe!

376
00:24:22,630 --> 00:24:26,400
In the same way that you find hope 
by believing in another's strength,

377
00:24:26,400 --> 00:24:30,060
I believe that everyone always remains weak!

378
00:24:30,060 --> 00:24:33,890
So weak and fragile that, other than 
clinging to just one precious thing,

379
00:24:33,890 --> 00:24:37,280
they aren't even capable of 
fulfilling their own desires!

380
00:24:37,280 --> 00:24:39,120
That's what I believe!

381
00:24:39,520 --> 00:24:43,440
For 400 years, I have loved only one woman.

382
00:24:43,440 --> 00:24:46,170
That is far longer than the 
time we spent together.

383
00:24:46,170 --> 00:24:48,430
And even after being 
without her for so long,

384
00:24:48,430 --> 00:24:50,800
her image is forever burned into me.

385
00:24:51,140 --> 00:24:54,460
It never stops burning my very soul!

386
00:24:56,160 --> 00:24:59,810
My heart is still in pieces, 
as it has been since the day we parted.

387
00:25:00,130 --> 00:25:02,560
Nothing has changed for me!

388
00:25:04,670 --> 00:25:06,520
I'll say it one more time.

389
00:25:06,740 --> 00:25:09,650
I still have the advantage.

390
00:25:09,650 --> 00:25:13,090
And if parts of our stories 
don't match, what then?

391
00:25:13,780 --> 00:25:18,170
For both you and me, so long as 
that one crucial person remains,

392
00:25:18,170 --> 00:25:19,870
the battle will never end.

393
00:25:20,370 --> 00:25:22,640
Don't underestimate Emilia.

394
00:25:22,640 --> 00:25:25,860
She won't go along with your ideas anymore.

395
00:25:25,860 --> 00:25:27,370
She'll overcome it all!

396
00:25:27,370 --> 00:25:29,330
You really think that's possible?

397
00:25:29,330 --> 00:25:33,050
She'll be stranded with nowhere to go,
 her own regrets will crush her,

398
00:25:33,050 --> 00:25:36,230
she'll be sorry she ever aspired to change,

399
00:25:36,230 --> 00:25:38,400
and she'll cling to you in tears.

400
00:25:38,400 --> 00:25:39,620
That's what suits—

401
00:25:39,620 --> 00:25:42,700
Crying doesn't suit any woman!

402
00:25:42,700 --> 00:25:47,050
I've never seen a girl who 
sucked that bad at crying!

403
00:25:47,050 --> 00:25:49,480
She will be hurt and held in contempt.

404
00:25:49,480 --> 00:25:51,940
That is the fate of the half-elf.

405
00:25:52,360 --> 00:25:56,720
Born with the curse of sharing the 
same lineage as the Witch of Envy,

406
00:25:56,720 --> 00:26:00,120
it's inevitable that she 
will be scorned as a witch!

407
00:26:00,700 --> 00:26:02,300
Screw you!

408
00:26:02,300 --> 00:26:04,100
How the hell is she a witch?!

409
00:26:04,100 --> 00:26:07,370
You're the ones ganging up 
on her to make her one!

410
00:26:07,730 --> 00:26:11,040
Has anyone ever even told her

411
00:26:11,040 --> 00:26:14,290
that it's okay to cry if she's hurt or sad?!

412
00:26:14,290 --> 00:26:18,260
If she can't wipe her own tears away, 
someone outside will dry them for her!

413
00:26:18,500 --> 00:26:24,270
Has anyone ever told her that there's 
someone out there who'll do that for her?!

414
00:26:24,820 --> 00:26:27,500
If no one else will do it, I will!

415
00:26:27,860 --> 00:26:28,890
Feelings...

416
00:26:29,460 --> 00:26:30,700
Curses...

417
00:26:30,700 --> 00:26:33,730
If you believe they're things 
that can never change,

418
00:26:33,730 --> 00:26:35,780
we'll just pound the truth into you!

419
00:26:36,630 --> 00:26:39,130
My name is Natsuki Subaru!

420
00:26:39,130 --> 00:26:42,990
I am the silver-haired 
half-elf Emilia's knight!

421
00:26:46,980 --> 00:26:49,460
Emilia's coming, Roswaal.

422
00:26:49,720 --> 00:26:53,000
That girl you're so convinced is weak

423
00:26:53,000 --> 00:26:56,270
is gonna come to sever that 
last desire of yours!

424
00:26:57,480 --> 00:27:01,430
So my suspicions were correct, Natsuki Subaru.

425
00:27:01,780 --> 00:27:02,990
What?

426
00:27:02,990 --> 00:27:05,450
You and I are alike...

427
00:27:06,610 --> 00:27:10,470
in the sense that we both force our 
ideals upon the women we love.

428
00:27:10,960 --> 00:27:14,900
You believe in weakness, 
and I believe in strength.

429
00:27:15,620 --> 00:27:19,920
I will agree on the point 
that you and I are alike.

430
00:27:22,450 --> 00:27:23,380
Let's go.

431
00:27:28,330 --> 00:27:32,330
The Beginning of the Sanctuary
and the Beginning of the End

432
00:27:28,910 --> 00:27:30,770
Stupid idiot!

433
00:27:42,040 --> 00:27:44,320
Right. I'm fine now.

434
00:27:55,040 --> 00:27:57,630
Welcome back, Emilia-sama.

435
00:27:57,630 --> 00:28:07,630


